            <ArticleTitle>Stimulation of the medial plantar nerve for complex regional pain syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1421-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2010.03.030</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 47-year old male with complex regional pain syndrome II in the distribution of the medial plantar nerve following metatarsal fracture, which was treated with peripheral nerve stimulation. Using a new technique of nerve stimulation with a percutaneous-type electrode, the patient experienced sustained relief at 12 months follow-up. To our knowledge, this is the first report of peripheral neurostimulation effectively managing pain for the medial plantar nerve.</AbstractText>
